---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Mentoring & communication — apprenti.dev Docs">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold">
                Mentoring & communication
            </h1>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">
            <section>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Beyond reviewing submissions, mentors and apprentices
                    need to talk about the work itself — a stuck point, a
                    piece of feedback, a request for a closer look at some
                    code. apprenti.dev handles this the same way it handles
                    everything else: no server, Git as the record, encrypted
                    at the application level so privacy doesn't depend
                    solely on the repository being private.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    How it stays serverless and private
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Messages are written as immutable objects on a dedicated
                    <code>apprenti/communication</code> branch, kept separate
                    from curriculum history. Nothing is transmitted, though,
                    unless every one of these holds:
                </p>
                <ul class="space-y-1 text-muted-foreground mt-2">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>The
                        repository's privacy has been <strong
                            >positively verified</strong
                        > as private (not just assumed) — public, internal,
                        and "unknown" all count as <em>not</em> private
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Your identity
                        and membership are valid
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>The recipient's
                        encryption key is available
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>The message's
                        signature validates
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    If a repository's visibility ever changes to public
                    mid-project, sync stops immediately: your local drafts
                    and history stay available, but nothing more is pushed
                    or pulled until it's private again.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    What you can do
                </h2>
                <ul class="space-y-1 text-muted-foreground mt-2">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span><strong
                            >Threads</strong
                        > — grouped conversations, tied to a task, a commit, a
                        branch, or a file when relevant
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span><strong
                            >Feedback</strong
                        > — structured mentor feedback with an optional category
                        (architecture, correctness, readability, testing, performance,
                        security, learning) and severity
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span><strong
                            >Help requests</strong
                        > — an apprentice can send <strong
                            >I need help</strong
                        > with a free-text description and automatically attach
                        the current task, branch, and commit, so you get the context
                        without them retyping it
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span><strong
                            >Ask Mentor about…</strong
                        > actions surface throughout the app — about a task, a
                        file, a selection of code, or a commit — so a question
                        always arrives with the right context already attached
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    Formal code review stays where it belongs
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    apprenti.dev does not reinvent Pull Requests or Merge
                    Requests. <strong>Request code review</strong> opens a
                    real PR on GitHub or a real MR on GitLab and links it
                    into the conversation — the mentorship layer is for the
                    surrounding conversation, not a competing review tool.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    Working offline
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Reading history, drafting messages, and sending a help
                    request all work with no network. A draft is only
                    queued to sync once the required encryption material is
                    in place; nothing is ever pushed before the repository's
                    privacy is (re-)verified, including a second check
                    immediately before the final push, in case something
                    changed mid-sync.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 flex gap-4">
            <a href="/docs" class="text-sm text-link hover:underline"
                >← All Docs</a
            >
            <a href="/" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:underline"
                >Back to apprenti.dev</a
            >
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
